        "number": 3,
        "instructionsHtml": "Section 3<p>Listen and answer questions 21–30.</p>",
        "groups": [
          {
            "id": "part-3-group-1",
            "type": "mcq",
            "selectCount": 1,
            "rubricHtml": "<h3>Questions 21–25</h3><p>Choose the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong> or <strong>C</strong>.</p>",
            "questions": [
              {
                "number": 21,
                "textHtml": "What does Trevor find interesting about the purpose of children's literature?",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "the fact that authors may not realise what values they're teaching"
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "the fact that literature can be entertaining and educational at the same time"
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "the fact that adults expect children to imitate characters in literature"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 22,
                "textHtml": "Trevor says the module about the purpose of children's literature made him",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "analyse some of the stories that his niece reads."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "wonder how far popularity reflects good quality."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "decide to start writing some children's stories."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 23,
                "textHtml": "Stephanie is interested in the Pictures module because",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "she intends to become an illustrator."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "she can remember beautiful illustrations from her childhood."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "she believes illustrations are more important than words."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 24,
                "textHtml": "Trevor and Stephanie agree that comics",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "are inferior to books."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "have the potential for being useful."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "discourage children from using their imagination."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 25,
                "textHtml": "With regard to books aimed at only boys or only girls, Trevor was surprised",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "how long the distinction had gone unquestioned."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "how few books were aimed at both girls and boys."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "how many children enjoyed books intended for the opposite sex."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
